sider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Morgan Stanley Direct Lending Fund is a business development company. It is a Private Debt fund. The fund specializes in senior secured term loans, first lien senior secureds (including unitranche loans), floating rate loans and second-lien senior secured term loans. The fund specializes in mezzanine debt, joint venture, unsecured debt, equity investments, leveraged buyouts, acquisitions, debt refinancings, recapitalizations and other opportunistic asset purchases. The fund chiefly invests in riskier bonds, issued by middle-market companies or by private equity firms looking to finance their acquisitions. The fund seeks to invest in software, IT services, insurance services, commercial services & supplies, health care providers & services, diversified consumer services, professional services, real estate management & development, automobile components and financial services. The fund seeks to invest in the United States. The fund seeks to invest in companies with EBITDA between $15 million and $200 million.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael  Occi Jr. | CEO & Interested Director | Age 41","financial_summary":["Morgan Stanley Direct Lending Fund is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.2B market cap.","Management returns a meaningful 19.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 3700% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text"